  "content": "Mason Rivers is losing less on the greens than Cole Bennett over each of their last 5 recorded rounds.\n\n- **Strokes gained putting**: Rivers averages -3.45 strokes/round (July 4–10, 5 rounds); Bennett averages -5.86 strokes/round (July 2–10, 5 rounds). Both are negative — each round measured cost both players strokes relative to the field on the green — but Bennett's deficit is noticeably larger.\n- **Putts per round**: Rivers averages 32.8; Bennett averages 34.0, over the same 5-round samples. Bennett's worst round in this stretch was 38 putts (July 3); Rivers's worst was 35 (July 4).\n\nNote the windows differ slightly in date range (Rivers's five rounds run July 4–10, Bennett's run July 2–10) since each is simply that player's own last five recorded rounds, not a shared calendar window.",
